2026-10-11T05:40:08.3960692Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4061404Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4071672Z [0m
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4072366Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4073226Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4073605Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4074466Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4075484Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4076043Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4076560Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4077291Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4077600Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4078457Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4079571Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4080951Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4081384Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4081577Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4081861Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4082383Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4082699Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4083149Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4083294Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4083436Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4083614Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4084057Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4084763Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4085139Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4085309Z I will:
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4085508Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4085852Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4086565Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4087297Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4087953Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4088404Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4088836Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4089260Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4089636Z    /root
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4101918Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4102642Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4115227Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4116218Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4116750Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4117397Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4118091Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4137686Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4138351Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4161242Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4162460Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4163197Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4163427Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4163606Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4163839Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4164103Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4164546Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4164755Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4164862Z If you would like to
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4165149Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4165318Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4165528Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4165874Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4166056Z 
2026-10-11T05:40:08.4166071Z 
